lines+=['','## Allocation, limitations and reproducibility','',f'Completed allocation: **{hours:.5f} GPU-hours** across {len(done)} terminal jobs. The registered finite cumulative ceiling is {ceiling:.5f} GPU-hours; it is an accounting limit for this batch, not a user-imposed total cap. Failed numerical recipes are included. Active/pending ledger entries: '+(', '.join(f"{x['name']} ({x['id']})" for x in active) or 'none')+'.','', 'All owned jobs use isolated paths, A10080GB preflight, float64 and highest matrix precision. At most two owned GPU jobs run concurrently. The branch is `exp/2026-11-17-burgers-quadtree`, backed up through `codeonly/exp/2026-11-17-burgers-quadtree`; no implementation merge occurred. Raw outputs, trained weights, checksums, source commits and failures are retained. Large derived arrays remain explicitly remote-only where indicated by retention manifests.','', 'No final-test, wider-seed, output-size scaling, five-dense-output or host-transfer superiority claim follows from these development panels. Those confirmation panels remain gated by a feasible accuracy/cost candidate. The bounded quadtree replaces refined parents and selects a fixed tree from initial data; it does not demonstrate online temporal refinement or state transfer. Failure of these finite recipes does not exclude other neural architectures, adaptive solvers or PDE regimes.','', 'Reproduce report tables with the implementation lane’s `reports/build_report.py --publish`; numerical drivers, prospective amendments and `cluster/ledger.json` identify the inputs and jobs. The evidence snapshot beside this report and its SHA manifest make the reported values auditable.','', '## Glossary','', '- **Projection:** best fitted coefficients for a known reference field; a representation diagnostic, not a forecast.\n- **PDE solve / rollout:** advance the prescribed initial field using the governing differential equation.\n- **ROM / NM-ROM:** reduced-order model / nonlinear-manifold reduced-order model.\n- **POD:** a linear basis fitted to training snapshots.\n- **Encoder:** network that maps a field to latent coordinates; optimized projection additionally adjusts those coordinates.\n- **Quadrature / integration order:** numerical sampling used to evaluate the weak PDE operator.\n- **Half-step / finer-grid change:** change after refining time or spatial evaluation; separate from reference error.\n- **Reference uncertainty:** conditional error estimate from independent convergent space/time ladders.\n- **Worst error:** maximum across the prescribed evolved times and cases, normalized by each initial reference norm.\n- **Warm query:** repeated solve after reusable compilation/cache preparation. Cold and setup costs remain separate.\n- **Time ratio:** ROM time divided by eligible classical time; below one is faster.\n- **Case bootstrap:** resampling whole trajectories to estimate uncertainty in the median paired ratio.\n- **Coordinates / rank:** number of active reduced coefficients.\n- **FamilyA / familyB:** the registered Gaussian and more localized boundary-compatible Burgers populations.\n- **Development / final test:** data used for architecture selection / untouched data reserved for frozen confirmation.\n- **Quadtree:** a square partition whose cells can be divided into four children.\n- **GPU-hour:** one allocated GPU for one hour, including setup and failed recipes.']
